{"reviewer_participant_id": "actor:stage2-cross-model-fable-01", "reviews": [{"case_id": "case:b036fd64c647dfd93e35", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "reconciled_stage1_candidate_ids": [], "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The stated scientific task defines the target quantity as a conditional (subset-scoped) rate, not a complete-domain rate over all scheduled stations.", "observed_value": "conditional-on-screen question", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Build a coastal-station workflow whose scientific question is the occurrence rate conditional on passing a prespecified signal screen."}]}, {"description": "The report explicitly declares the target population as the 72 signal-eligible stations, and the selected result is scoped to exactly that population.", "observed_value": "72-station target; claim scoped 'Among signal-eligible stations'", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 4, "end_line": 4, "quoted_text": "Target population: 72 signal-eligible stations that passed the prespecified signal screen."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Among signal-eligible stations, the occurrence rate was 18/72 = 25%."}]}, {"description": "The input data semantics match the computation: 18 eligible occurrences plus 54 eligible non-occurrences equals 72 eligible stations, and the 24 outside stations are marked not_assessed and are outside the claimed domain.", "observed_value": "18 + 54 = 72; 24 outside eligible set", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 4, "quoted_text": "accounting_group,station_count,occurrence_status\nsignal_eligible_occurrence,18,observed\nsignal_eligible_no_occurrence,54,not_observed\noutside_signal_eligible,24,not_assessed"}]}, {"description": "The producer line constructs the selected result with numerator and denominator both scoped to the signal-eligible population (18/72), matching the subset-scoped claim.", "observed_value": "18/72 = 25%", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "RESULT_LINE = f'[selected-result] Among signal-eligible stations, the occurrence rate was {OCCURRENCES}/{SIGNAL_ELIGIBLE_STATIONS} = {RATE_PERCENT}%.' + LF"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The report mentions a larger 96-station scheduled network, which could suggest a complete domain of 96 stations broader than the 72 used in the computation.", "observed_value": "96 scheduled stations mentioned", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 3, "end_line": 3, "quoted_text": "Scheduled network: 96 stations."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 5, "quoted_text": "Planned-unit accounting: 18 eligible stations with an occurrence, 54 eligible stations without an occurrence, and 24 scheduled stations outside the eligible set and not assessed for occurrence."}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted to establish that the selected result claims a complete-domain (96-station) quantity while computing over the 72-station retained subset. The attempt fails: the selected result at results/report.md line 8 is explicitly scoped 'Among signal-eligible stations', the declared target population at line 4 is the 72 signal-eligible stations, and task.md line 1 defines the scientific question as conditional on passing the screen. The 96-station network at line 3 is contextual accounting, not the claim domain; the 24 outside stations are declared 'not_assessed' and outside the claimed population. Claim domain and computation domain coincide (72), so the in-scope issue is absent.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:35069763f06891dba5a3", "verdict": "demonstrated_issue", "bounded_statement": "The selected result claims an occurrence rate 'for the entire scheduled survey network', whose complete domain per the report's own stated target population and the task is all 96 scheduled stations, but the computation divides 18 occurrences by only the 72 stations retained after the signal screen (18/72 = 0.25), excluding the 24 screen-omitted scheduled stations from the exposure denominator; the complete-domain computation would be 18/96 = 0.1875.", "root_cause": "The producer hard-codes SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS = 72 as the divisor in the selected-result line while the claim text asserts the entire scheduled survey network and the report declares the 96-station target population; the 24 omitted scheduled stations (occurrence_flag NA in the input) are silently dropped from the exposure base, with the report explicitly stating no protocol amendment or approved deviation exists and no conditional restatement of the claim to the retained subset.", "issue_class": "issue-class:retained-subset-for-complete-domain", "reconciled_stage1_candidate_ids": ["root-cause-candidate:24bfbbe68d18a3b9c640", "root-cause-candidate:46d9da91114c2361ff6c", "root-cause-candidate:a657354cae20642d2e01", "root-cause-candidate:5fba530c20ec7a2c0d19"], "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The task and the report's stated scientific target define the complete domain as the entire scheduled network of 96 stations.", "observed_value": "complete domain = 96 scheduled stations", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Build a compact coastal-station workflow that reports one occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 4, "end_line": 4, "quoted_text": "Target population: all 96 scheduled coastal stations in the survey network."}]}, {"description": "The selected result asserts a complete-network claim yet computes 18/72 using the retained-subset denominator, as the report itself states in the denominator line.", "observed_value": "18/72 = 0.25 claimed for entire network", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 14, "end_line": 14, "quoted_text": "Exposure denominator: the 72 stations retained after the signal screen."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 15, "end_line": 15, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network: 18 occurrences divided by 72 retained stations = 0.25 (25.00 occurrences per 100 stations)."}]}, {"description": "The producer code hard-codes the retained-subset count as the divisor in the selected-result line while labeling the quantity a rate for the entire scheduled survey network.", "observed_value": "SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS = 72 used as divisor", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 7, "end_line": 7, "quoted_text": "SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS = 72"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 23, "end_line": 23, "quoted_text": "SELECTED_LINE = f'[selected-result] Occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network: {OBSERVED_OCCURRENCES} occurrences divided by {SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS} retained stations = {SELECTED_RATE_FRACTION} ({SELECTED_RATE_PERCENT} occurrences per 100 stations).' + LF"}]}, {"description": "The input data shows all 96 stations are scheduled units, with omitted stations still scheduled (scheduled=yes) but carrying NA occurrence flags; e.g., the first omitted row.", "observed_value": "96 scheduled rows; omitted rows scheduled=yes, occurrence_flag=NA", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "station_id,region,scheduled,screen_status,omission_reason,occurrence_flag"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 5, "quoted_text": "CS-004,North,yes,omitted,screen_fail_low_snr,NA"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 97, "end_line": 97, "quoted_text": "CS-096,Outer,yes,omitted,screen_fail_data_gap,NA"}]}, {"description": "The report explicitly rules out any protocol amendment or approved deviation that could legitimize substituting the retained subset for the complete domain.", "observed_value": "no amendment/deviation", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "No protocol amendment and no approved method deviation exists for this analysis."}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The report transparently discloses the 72-station denominator and the 24 omitted stations, which could be read as an implicit conditional restatement narrowing the claim to the retained subset.", "observed_value": "denominator disclosed", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 10, "end_line": 10, "quoted_text": "Stations omitted by the signal screen: 24"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 14, "end_line": 14, "quoted_text": "Exposure denominator: the 72 stations retained after the signal screen."}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted to falsify the demonstrated issue by reading the disclosed 72-station exposure-denominator line (report line 14) as narrowing the claim to the retained subset. This fails: the selected result itself (line 15) explicitly asserts the rate is 'for the entire scheduled survey network', the stated target population (line 4) and task.md both fix the complete domain at 96 scheduled stations, and line 18 states no amendment or approved deviation exists. I also checked whether the data could make the domains coincide: inputs/data.csv shows 96 scheduled rows with 24 omitted-but-scheduled stations (occurrence_flag NA), so the retained subset (72) is strictly smaller than the claimed complete domain (96). The mismatch between claim domain (96) and computation domain (72) is directly entailed by the visible files.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:2e26bf5ece15be03717f", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "reconciled_stage1_candidate_ids": [], "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The task requests a rate for the entire scheduled survey network, and the report declares the complete 96-station domain as its target.", "observed_value": "complete domain = 96 scheduled stations", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Using the supplied coastal-station base workflow, produce a revised selected occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 4, "end_line": 4, "quoted_text": "Target population: all 96 scheduled coastal stations in the survey network."}]}, {"description": "The selected result uses the complete 96-station scheduled domain as the exposure denominator, matching the complete-network claim: 18/96 = 0.1875.", "observed_value": "18/96 = 0.1875", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 14, "end_line": 14, "quoted_text": "Exposure denominator: all 96 scheduled stations, so the 24 omitted stations stay in the denominator and contribute zero observed occurrences."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 15, "end_line": 15, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Occurrence rate over the complete scheduled network: 18 occurrences divided by 96 scheduled stations = 0.1875 (18.75 occurrences per 100 scheduled stations)."}]}, {"description": "The producer code constructs the selected result with SCHEDULED_STATIONS = 96 as the divisor, i.e., the complete domain, not the 72-station retained subset.", "observed_value": "divisor = SCHEDULED_STATIONS (96)", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 6, "end_line": 6, "quoted_text": "SCHEDULED_STATIONS = 96"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 23, "end_line": 23, "quoted_text": "SELECTED_LINE = f'[selected-result] Occurrence rate over the complete scheduled network: {OBSERVED_OCCURRENCES} occurrences divided by {SCHEDULED_STATIONS} scheduled stations = {NETWORK_RATE_FRACTION} ({NETWORK_RATE_PERCENT} occurrences per 100 scheduled stations).' + LF"}]}, {"description": "The report explicitly and conditionally restates the epistemic status of the complete-domain figure given the 24 unobserved stations, framing it as a lower bound, and affirms no subset denominator is used anywhere.", "observed_value": "lower-bound caveat; 96-only denominators", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "The 24 omitted stations were never observed, so the complete-network rate above is a lower bound on the true network rate."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 19, "end_line": 19, "quoted_text": "No screened-subset rate is reported; every claim in this report uses the complete 96 station denominator."}]}, {"description": "The input data confirms 96 scheduled stations (one row each plus header), consistent with the 96-station denominator used.", "observed_value": "96 scheduled rows", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "station_id,region,scheduled,screen_status,omission_reason,occurrence_flag"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 97, "end_line": 97, "quoted_text": "CS-096,Outer,yes,omitted,screen_fail_data_gap,NA"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The numerator of 18 occurrences is observed only among the 72 retained stations, so one component of the computation derives from the retained subset; the 24 omitted stations have NA occurrence flags in the data rather than observed zeros.", "observed_value": "numerator observed on retained subset only", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 11, "end_line": 11, "quoted_text": "Occurrences observed among the retained stations: 18"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 5, "quoted_text": "CS-004,North,yes,omitted,screen_fail_low_snr,NA"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted to demonstrate the in-scope issue via the numerator: the 18 occurrences are observed only among the 72 retained stations while the 24 omitted stations are NA, so one could argue the computation still rests on a retained subset. This attempt fails within scope: the scope concerns claiming a complete-domain quantity while computing over only a retained subset, and here the exposure denominator is the full 96-station domain (report lines 14-15; analysis.py line 23), the zero-contribution treatment of the 24 omitted stations is explicitly disclosed (line 14), and the claim is conditionally restated as a lower bound on the true network rate (line 18). The claimed domain and the computation's domain coincide at 96 stations, so the in-scope issue is absent.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}]}